    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="5" relname="span">Sånga Säby Kursgård, Sweden, will be the site of the 1969 International Conference on Computational Linguistics, September 1-4.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">It is expected that some 250 linguists will attend from Asia, West Europe, East Europe including Russia, and the United States.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="5" relname="elaboration">The conference will be concerned with the application of mathematical and computer techniques to the study of natural languages, the development of computer programs as tools for linguistic research; and the application of linguistics to the development of man-machine communication systems.</segment>
        <group id="4" type="span"/>
        <group id="5" type="span" parent="4" relname="span"/>
    </body>
</rst>
